		<item>
			<title>Sci-Tech Complex</title>
			<link>http://koreanfriendship.org/dprk-information/19-sci-tech-complex</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="true">http://koreanfriendship.org/dprk-information/19-sci-tech-complex</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>A magnificent the Sci-Tec Complex, a centre for dissemination of up-to-date science and technology, was built on the beautiful Ssuk Island on the Taedong in the capital city Pyongyang under the personal initiative and energetic leadership of respected Marshal <strong>Kim Jong Un</strong>.</p>
<p>With a shape of a gigantic structure of an atom it sits on a total floor space of over 106,600㎡.</p>
<p>It is a masterpiece of architecture with its unique beauty and perfect figurative artistic representation and a national treasure demonstrating in a panoramic view the level of architecture of Korea.</p>
<p>The façade in the main hall has a mosaic mural portraying the great leaders of the Korean people Comrade <strong>Kim II Sung</strong> and Comrade <strong>Kim Jong II</strong> who devoted their lifetime to the country and people.</p>
<p>It is a comprehensive e-library that can serve the materials of the recent technological achievements at home and those of advanced science and technology abroad as well as the books of science and technology published in Korea in the past, all electronically processed in a comprehensive and systematic way.</p>
<p>It is furnished with massive databases and many e-reading rooms so that anybody can have an access to the materials as they wish, and gives also a real-time IT service via the domestic computer network to all the scientific research sectors, educational institutions, factories and enterprises as well as to the private homes.</p>
<p>There are various halls like of children’s dream, of fundamental science and technology, of an applied science and technology, of experiencing earthquake, a virtual laboratory, an indoor sci-tech exhibition by sectors and other reading rooms and places.</p>
<p>On display in each room are the visual aids, relief maps and models of equipment so that the visitors can learn the knowledge handling them personally.</p>
<p>Outdoors, there are an open-air exhibition of science and technology divided into the districts of future energy and science games, open-air study site, fountain park, a unique tower symbolizing science and technology and 500-capacity hotel that is furnished with all the conveniences and goes well with the surroundings.</p>
<p>Besides, what is characteristic is its emphasis on the energy-saving economy and green-orientation. The lighting and air-conditioning are based on the solar heat and geo-therm.</p>
<p>As is seen, the Sci-Tec Complex is good evidence showing the great emphasis on the science and technology and the level of their development in Korea.</p>]]></description>
			<category>DPRK Information</category>
			<pubDate>Fri, 21 Oct 2016 09:43:51 +0000</pubDate>
		</item>
		<item>
			<title>Pigo(A Flying Vehicle)</title>
			<link>http://koreanfriendship.org/dprk-information/18-pigo-a-flying-vehicle</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="true">http://koreanfriendship.org/dprk-information/18-pigo-a-flying-vehicle</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p>Pigo is a world-first military glider invented by the Korean people. It is meant by a flying vehicle. It was made in 1592 and used for a military correspondence.</p>
<p>The old Korean historical records say that it had a shape of an eagle. It is composed of wings, a tail, head part, four-man seat, pockets to store wind, bellows for raising wind and a rope for steering the main wing and tail wing.</p>
<p>It had also wheels at the bottom so as to run and move on the ground.</p>
<p>The hull and wings were made of wood covered with hides. The wind pockets in the hull, made of hides, were filled with compressed air. At the bottom of the pockets there is a door capping the hole. When the door is hammered to open, the compressed air is burst forth downwards through the hole, generating reaction and buoyancy enough to take off.</p>
<p>At the same time the four men pull the rope with full force to move the wings up and down. Then thePigo rises up off the surface, moving forward.</p>
<p>In general it could glide approximately 300m far. In an updraft it could fly about 12 kms.</p>
<p>It is said that in 1592 when Japanese aggressors invaded Korea by surprise the Korean army in a siege flew a manned Pigo to inform of the invasion to the superior authorities 12 km away.</p>
<p>The manufacture and use of such a flying vehicle like a Pigo already in so earlier time is a great pride of the Korean nation.</p>
<p>Leonardo Da Vinci had an idea of a flying vehicle with its wings fluttered by force of feet and steered by hand, but not applied in practice.</p>
<p>In the middle ages Chinese and Germans too had a conception on a glider, but not in practice.</p>
<p>Indeed, Pigo was not only a distinct demonstration of the wisdom and talent of the Korean nation, but also is a significant invention in the annals of world aviation.</p>]]></description>
