		<item>
			<title>Historic Congresses of WPK</title>
			<link>http://koreanfriendship.org/dprk-information/17-historic-congresses-of-wpk</link>
			<guid isPermaLink="true">http://koreanfriendship.org/dprk-information/17-historic-congresses-of-wpk</guid>
			<description><![CDATA[<p><strong><span lang="EN-US">- Congress for the founding of the Central Organizing Committee of the North Korean Communist Party(October, 1945)</span></strong></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">President <strong>Kim II Sung</strong> organized Party organizations in the local places immediately after the liberation in reliance on the successes and experience personally achieved during the anti-Japanese revolutionary struggle before he convened the Congress for the founding of the Central Organizing Committee of the Communist Party of North Korea on the 10th of October, 1945.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Congress brought under deliberation the issues of founding the central organizing committee of the Communist Party of North Korea and its correctness, the organizational and political lines of the Party and the principles of the Party building as proposed by President <strong style="font-size: 12.16px;">Kim II Sung</strong> and agreed upon them and set forth a challenge on turning the northern half of Korea into a formidable revolutionary base through carrying out the four impending tasks for founding a democratic people’s republic without delay.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">It formed the Central Organizing Committee of the Communist Party of North Korea, a central leading organ of the Party in accordance with the guideline put forward by him and announced it to the world.</span></p>
<p>In August, 1946 the Communist Party of North Korea developed into the Workers’ Party, a unified party of the working masses, according to the line of building a popular party, where he, the founder and leader of the Party, was elected to its head.</p>
<p>With the founding of a working-class Party guided by Juche idea the Korean people could propell the building of a new society with a great confidence under the leadership of the Party.</p>
<p> </p>
<p>- <strong>Second Congress of the Workers’Party of North Korea</strong> (March, 1948)</p>
<p>-The Second Congress of the Workers’ Party of North Korea met at a time when the people’s power was consolidated under the wise leadership of President <strong>Kim II Sung</strong>, the national economy thriving, regular revolutionary armed forces founded and the Party ranks rapidly expanded as the policy of building a popular party was fully implemented.</p>
<p>  In the Congress President <strong>Kim Il Sung</strong> reviewed the obtaining domestic and international situations and put forward important tasks that would serve as a guideline for opposing the US imperialists’ moves for a separate election and rig-up of a puppet regime and reunifying the country peacefully and implementing the qualitative consolidation of the Party regarding it as a pivotal issue in the building of a popular party.</p>
<p>In his concluding speech he emphasized on the strengthening of the struggle against factionalism and instructed to root out all the factional hangovers within the Party and build up the unity and cohesion of the Party.</p>
<p>The Congress elected the Central Committee of the Party headed by President <strong style="font-size: 12.16px;">Kim II Sung</strong><span style="font-size: 12.16px;">.</span></p>
<p>It marked a new turn in fortifying the unity and cohesion of the Party led by President <strong style="font-size: 12.16px;">Kim II Sung</strong> and consolidating the Workers’ Party of Korea.</p>
<p> </p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">- <strong>Third Congress of WPK</strong> (April, 1956)</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Third Congress of the WPK is a historic one which reviewed the glorious struggle and the victorious path traversed by the WPK under the leadership of President <strong style="font-size: 12.16px;">Kim II Sung</strong> and put forth a strategy for the completion of building the foundations of socialism.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">It was convened at a time when it was urgent to complete the all-round socialist transformation of production relations and to frustrate the imperialist manoevres for a new war and tide over the revisionism sneaked in the international communist movement to push forward the world revolution.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In the Congress President <strong style="font-size: 12.16px;">Kim II Sung</strong> set forth Five-Year Plan for completing the socialist transformation of the production relations and the Development of the National Economy to build up the foundations of the socialist industrialization and the task for continuously consolidating and developing the Democratic Front for the Reunification of Korea, people’s power and the state and social system.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">   In addition, he put forth important tasks for strengthening the struggle against factionalism since the factional remnants were still lingering within the Party, further stabilizing the unity and cohesion of the Party and improving the organizational and ideological work of the Party.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">It was a historical congress which solemnly declared within and without the deeper the revolution and construction develop in depth and the more complicated the situation at home and abroad turns, the firmer the Party membership rally behind President Kim Il Sung to hold fast to the banner of Juche and revolutionary principles.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US"> </span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">- <strong>Fourth Congress of WPK</strong> (September, 1961)</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The historic Fourth Congress of the WPK summed up the brilliant successes achieved in the revolution and construction and put forward a grand programme for achieving a high goal of the socialist construction.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">It opened at a time when it was urgent to expound the tasks of the Korean revolution to conform to the new demands of the revolutionary development and work out new strategic and tactical policies for hastening the revolution in south Korea and the reunification of the country and accelerating the world revolution.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">President <strong>Kim II Sung</strong> presented in the Congress the task of carrying out the First Seven-Year Plan for reaching the high goal of socialism and illumined the characteristics of the south Korean revolution and fighting tasks on the basis of the scientific analysis of the south Korean revolution.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In addition, he suggested important tasks of continuing to strengthen the Party organizationally and ideologically, in particular, opposing the revisionism, factionalism, localism and nepotism and defending the unity of the Party in ideology and purpose.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Congress unanimously approved his report and concluding speech and adopted appropriate decisions.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Fourth Congress of the WPK was a historic event in developing to a higher stage the struggle of the Korean people for the socialist construction and national reunification and the organizational and ideological unity of the Party ranks.</span></p>
<p> </p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">-<strong> 5th Congress of WPK</strong> (November, 1970)</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Fifth Congress of WPK reviewed the brilliant successes made in the struggle for the all-round victory of the Juche idea and put forward programmatic tasks of hastening the complete victory of socialism and the nation-wide victory of the revolution and steadfastly developing the Party.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">It met at a time when the tasks of the socialist industrialization were brilliantly brought into reality under the leadership of President <strong>Kim II Sung</strong> and a great advance was made in the work of establishing a Juche ideological system throughout the Party and society.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">He set forth in the Congress very important tasks including the main tasks of the socialist economic construction for the implementation of the Six-Year Plan, the tasks of socialist cultural construction and those of the defense build-up.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">In addition, he expounded the task of the development of the south Korean revolution, the policy on the national reunification and the independent foreign policy of the Party.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">He elucidated in the Congress the tasks of strengthening the monolithic ideological system within the Party and further consolidating it organizationally and ideologically and enhancing the leading role of the Party and defined the general task of the Party work.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Fifth Congress of the WPK served a momentum in laying a firmer organizational and ideological foundation of the Party, further strengthening it and opening up a new phase of the revolutionary development.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US"> </span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">- <strong>Sixth Congress of WPK</strong> (October, 1980)</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Six Congress of the WPK was a historic meeting which was held at a time when the Korean revolution entered a new phase under the sagacious leadership of President <strong>Kim Il Sung</strong> and the great leader Comrade<strong> Kim Jong II</strong> .</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">President <strong>Kim II Sung</strong> made an all-round review of the brilliant successes achieved in the revolution and construction under the leadership of the Party since the Fifth Congress of the Party and put forward fighting tasks of their implementation.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">He put forward militant tasks including the task of modeling the whole society on the Juche idea and the task of reaching the ten long-term goals of the socialist economic construction.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">Besides, he suggested a new proposal of the national reunification on establishing the Democratic Federal Republic of Koryo and the Party’s external policy approach and set forth very important tasks including the strengthening of the Party work.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Congress elected great leader Comrade<strong> Kim Jong II </strong>to the Member of the Presidium of the Political Bureau of the Central Committee of the Party, Member of the Party Central Military Commission and Secretary of the Central Committee of the Party reflecting the unanimous will and desire of the entire Party membership and the people.</span></p>
<p><span lang="EN-US">The Sixth Congress of the WPK served as a momentum in accelerating the complete victory of socialism and the cause of modeling the whole Party and society upon the Juche idea.</span></p>]]></description>
